    "result_text": "All 255 tests pass, including the new `AcceptanceTest.coreReturnsUnifiedMemberId`. **BUILD SUCCESS.**\n\n## Summary\n\nI unified `customerCode` and `membershipNumber` into a single `memberId` formatted `<REGION><FY><HASH8><CHK>`, and removed the standalone `checkDigit`.\n\n**What changed:**\n\n1. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 renamed the persisted field/column `customerCode`/`customer_code` \u2192 `memberId`/`member_id` (getter/setter updated).\n\n2. **`AssignOwnerMemberId.java`** (renamed from `AssignOwnerCustomerCode.java`) \u2014 now builds `region + fy + hash8(telephone+lastName)`, appends a single Luhn check digit computed over the digits of that base, and sets `memberId`. Collision de-duplication now compares against existing owners' `memberId`. `REGION` and `HASH8` (first 8 upper-hex of SHA-256 over normalized E.164 telephone + lastName) are unchanged; `FY` is the 2-digit fiscal year of the registrationDate (reusing `OwnerMapper.fiscalYearOf`).\n\n3. **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 the pipeline step `assignCustomerCode` \u2192 `assignMemberId` pointing at the new class.\n\n4. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 removed the `checkDigit` and `membershipNumber` mappings and their methods; `locality` now derives the region from the `memberId` prefix; `fiscalYear`/`ownerSegment`/`timezone` unchanged. `memberId` maps automatically by name.\n\n5. **`AuditOwnerCreated.java`** \u2014 the human-readable audit line now emits `memberId` (dropping `membershipNumber`), and `primaryIdentifier` returns `memberId`, so the structured event's value tracks the memberId (the JSON key is deliberately kept as `customerCode` for backward compatibility, as the original design documented).\n\n6. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 removed `customerCode`, `checkDigit`, `membershipNumber` schema properties; added a `memberId` property (so the generated `OwnerDto` reflects the new contract).\n\n7. **SQL schemas** (h2, hsqldb, mysql, postgres) \u2014 column `customer_code` \u2192 `member_id`, widened to `VARCHAR(32)` to accommodate the `UNKNOWN`-region + collision-suffix worst case.\n\nThe fiscal-year value, audit record, owner segment, and locality now all reference the unified `memberId`, and collision handling applies to it.",
